// =======================================================
// lnzip.cst — the barrel.
//
// Imports every module and defines nothing. Its only job is to be compiled
// with `caustic -c`, which type-checks the whole library the way a consumer
// linking it would, without needing a main. The test runner does exactly that
// before it builds any suite: a module that stops compiling is caught once,
// here, instead of once per test that happens to import it.
// =======================================================

use "core/errno.cst" as errno;
